System Relationships

                         Mage Skate
                             │
             ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐
             │                               │
        Core Systems                    User Interface
             │                               │
       Game Manager                   Title Screen / HUD
             │
       Level Manager
             │
       ┌─────┴──────────┐
       │                │
  2D Gameplay       3D Gameplay
       │                │
  Skate Movement    Exploration
       │                │
       └───────┬────────┘
               │
       Perspective Manager
               │
        Spellcasting System
               │
       ┌───────┴─────────┐
       │                 │
     Combat          World Puzzles
       │                 │
   Enemies/Bosses    Interactables
       │
  Health and Damage

World Progression

Elemental Tower
    ├── Level 1
    ├── Level 2
    └── Boss Level
          │
          ▼
Wicked Forest
    ├── Level 1
    ├── Level 2
    └── Boss Level
          │
          ▼
Lost Necropolis
    ├── Level 1
    ├── Level 2
    └── Boss Level

Each world contains two standard levels and one boss level, for a total of nine levels across three worlds.

Design Principles

* Modularity: Each major gameplay system has its own directory.
* Reusability: Shared scenes and components minimize duplicated logic.
* Separation of concerns: Gameplay logic, assets, scenes, and configuration resources are kept separate.
* Extensibility: New spells, enemies, bosses, and levels can be added without redesigning the entire project.
* Team collaboration: Developers can work on separate systems with clearly defined responsibilities.

Note: This document describes the planned project architecture. Some files may initially be empty placeholders and should be implemented as development progresses.
